## Create project {% #create-project %}

Head to the [AACSearch Console](https://cloud.aacsearch.io/console).

{% only_dark %}
![Create project screen](/images/docs/quick-starts/dark/create-project.png)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![Create project screen](/images/docs/quick-starts/create-project.png)
{% /only_light %}

If this is your first time using AACSearch, create an account and create your first project.

Then, under **Add a platform**, add a **Web app**. The **Hostname** should be localhost. 

{% only_dark %}
![Add a platform](/images/docs/quick-starts/dark/add-platform.png)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![Add a platform](/images/docs/quick-starts/add-platform.png)
{% /only_light %}

You can skip optional steps.

## Initialize AACSearch SDK {% #init-sdk %}

To use AACSearch in our Refine app, we'll need to find our project ID. Find your project's ID in the **Settings** page. 

{% only_dark %}
![Project settings screen](/images/docs/quick-starts/dark/project-id.png)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![Project settings screen](/images/docs/quick-starts/project-id.png)
{% /only_light %}

Navigate to `src/utility/aacsearchClient.ts` and add your API credentials.


```ts
import { Account, AACSearch, Storage } from "@refinedev/aacsearch";

const AACSEARCH_URL = '<YOUR_API_ENDPOINT>'; // Replace with your AACSearch API Endpoint
const AACSEARCH_PROJECT = "<PROJECT_ID>"; // Replace with your project ID

const aacsearchClient = new AACSearch();

aacsearchClient.setEndpoint(AACSEARCH_URL).setProject(AACSEARCH_PROJECT);
const account = new Account(aacsearchClient);
const storage = new Storage(aacsearchClient);

export { account, aacsearchClient, storage };

```